{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/pjsog6","slideIndex":3,"text":"Nouwens, M., Liccardi, I., Veale, M., Karger, D. and Kagal, L. (2020). Dark Patterns after the GDPR: Scraping Consent Pop-ups and Demonstrating their Influence. CHI 2020. https://doi.org/10.1145/3313831.3376321 ; https://arxiv.org/abs/2001.02479\nBollinger, D., Kubicek, K., Cotrini, C. and Basin, D. (2022). Automating Cookie Consent and GDPR Violation Detection. USENIX Security 2022, pp. 2893–2910. https://www.usenix.org/conference/usenixsecurity22/presentation/bollinger\nThe gap is scoped to these reviewed works. CookieBlock classifies cookies and enforces consent preferences; it does not evaluate the home-and-guest conversational experience proposed here. Do not claim that no gamified privacy system exists. The report’s F1/FIFA cases are interface examples, not controlled comparative studies."}
