{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/3qq6yh","slideIndex":4,"text":"Current code path: extension/popup.js collects metadata, a window.Cookiebot consent snapshot and rendered public declaration tables; it sends value-free inputs to the local server. src/engine/cookiebot-adapter.js normalises inputs. input-adapter.js matches purpose evidence and constructs guests. src/ui/app.js provides scenarios and chat. server.js uses Gemini to interpret messages and validates structured responses. rules.js validates and applies explicit intents to local state. Ambiguous responses should produce clarification without state changes; the browser UI returns to ask the user. Unknown-purpose matches remain unclassified. Dashed consent write-back is planned, not implemented. The full journey currently runs in the local website; the connector is already an extension."}
