{"kind":"table","id":"tb/m5s3m58n","slideIndex":6,"position":{"left":65,"top":250,"width":1150,"height":315},"name":"","rows":5,"cols":2,"preview":"Outcome | Proposed measure"}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/gjdpad","slideIndex":6,"text":"Proposed evaluation, not results. Pilot tasks before the main study. Compare the gamified journey with a category dashboard using matched privacy information and tasks; counterbalance order. Record initial stated preferences, then debrief apparent mismatches because learning can legitimately change preferences. Questionnaire agreement is a reference, not objective privacy truth. To isolate gamification from chatbot effects, use a simplified variant with the same choice logic if feasible; otherwise report results as a comparison of the full interfaces. Avoid invented sample sizes or targets; agree them before recruitment. Report comprehension, choice fidelity, errors, time, usability and engagement. A small sample gives exploratory evidence. Source: report Chapter 5 and proposed refinements for this presentation."}
